From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:23:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix socket 3 never linking, and lock the port once a battle
 starts

The auto-reset latch was set by (link_now && m_last_data_cmd != 0) and
never cleared, so it only had to be true once to disable auto-reset on
that port for the rest of the session.

XD reads the two sockets in sequence. Both Emeralds boot together with
the GameCube, so both open a link window a couple of seconds in, but XD
is still working on socket 2. Any stray data command to socket 3 during
that period leaves m_last_data_cmd set, and the coincident boot window
then latches socket 3 as established. Its auto-reset is switched off
before XD ever asks it anything, the window never reopens, and XD sits on
"checking connection" for socket 3 forever. That matches the report:
socket 2 links itself, socket 3 never does, in netplay and solo alike.

Three changes:

- Latch on link_now && handshake_active, so it takes a link window plus
  data that is actually flowing right now, not a link window plus the
  memory of a data command from some seconds ago.
- Add a permanent battle lock, set once 64 data commands have crossed the
  link. That only happens when XD has genuinely read a party, and nothing
  clears it: no auto-reset can fire for the rest of the session. Rebooting
  Emerald mid-battle drops the link and kills the fight with no message,
  so that has to be impossible rather than merely unlikely. A stray probe
  or a boot-time coincidence is a handful of commands and never gets near
  the threshold.
- Clear the (non-battle) latch when XD is probing again with no data for
  30 s, so a port can never stay wedged before a battle has started.

Also make the reset cooldown adaptive. The 6 s floor exists for the slow
official-BIOS boot (4.78 s vs the bundled BIOS's 2.35 s), but once a link
window has been observed since the last reset the core has demonstrably
booted, so the port can re-arm half a second after the window closes
instead of waiting out the worst case again.
---
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp | 73 ++++++++++++++++------
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h   |  5 ++
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
index 2f79ac4..63088ba 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
@@ -85,24 +85,62 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
         m_last_cmd == EBufferCommands::CMD_WRITE_GBA)
     {
       m_last_data_cmd = m_timestamp_sent;
+      if (m_data_cmd_count < DATA_CMDS_FOR_BATTLE)
+        ++m_data_cmd_count;
     }
 
     const u64 tps = static_cast<u64>(m_system.GetSystemTimers().GetTicksPerSecond());
     const bool link_now = m_core->IsLinkEnabled();
 
-    // Latch once the joybus link is up AND real data (READ/WRITE) has flowed:
-    // the party read is done and the battle is underway. Never auto-reset after
+    const bool probing = m_last_cmd == EBufferCommands::CMD_RESET ||
+                         m_last_cmd == EBufferCommands::CMD_STATUS;
+    const bool handshake_active =
+        m_last_data_cmd != 0 && (m_timestamp_sent - m_last_data_cmd) < tps * 8;
+
+    // Remember that a link window actually opened since the last reset: it
+    // proves the core finished booting, which lets the cooldown below re-arm
+    // promptly instead of waiting out the slowest possible boot again.
+    if (link_now)
+      m_window_seen_since_reset = true;
+
+    // Latch once the joybus link is up AND real data (READ/WRITE) is flowing:
+    // the party read is done and the battle is underway. Don't auto-reset after
     // this. Otherwise a rare coincidence during turn 1 -- Emerald briefly leaves
     // JOYBUS mode at the "Link standby -> battle scene" transition (link_now
     // false) while an 8s+ animation has let handshake_active lapse and a
     // STATUS/RESET probe lands in that window -- would satisfy the guard below
     // and reboot Emerald out from under XD, dropping the link and crashing the
-    // fight with no message. Pre-battle window-reopening is unaffected: during
-    // pure copyright-screen probing XD sends only STATUS/RESET, so m_last_data_cmd
-    // is still 0 and the brief JOYBUS blip does not trip the latch early.
-    if (link_now && m_last_data_cmd != 0)
+    // fight with no message.
+    //
+    // The data command must be RECENT. XD reads the two sockets in sequence, so
+    // the port it isn't working on yet can see an old stray data command and,
+    // seconds later, a boot-time link window; latching on that coincidence wedged
+    // the port for the rest of the session (auto-reset off, window never reopens,
+    // "checking connection" forever). That is the socket-3 detection failure.
+    if (link_now && handshake_active)
       m_link_established = true;
 
+    // Once this much traffic has crossed the link, XD has genuinely read a party
+    // and the battle is underway. From here the port is locked: no auto-reset
+    // for the rest of the session, and no recovery path may re-arm it. Rebooting
+    // Emerald mid-battle drops the link and kills the fight with no message, so
+    // that outcome must be impossible rather than merely unlikely. A stray probe
+    // or a boot-time coincidence is a handful of commands and never gets close.
+    if (m_data_cmd_count >= DATA_CMDS_FOR_BATTLE)
+      m_battle_locked = true;
+
+    // ...and the latch is not permanent. If XD is probing again with no data
+    // having flowed for half a minute, the battle this latch was protecting is
+    // over (or never started) and the port has to be recoverable. The threshold
+    // is deliberately far longer than the 8 s handshake window: in-battle
+    // animations can starve data commands for a while, and re-arming the reset
+    // mid-fight is exactly the crash the latch exists to prevent.
+    if (m_link_established && !m_battle_locked && probing && !link_now &&
+        (m_last_data_cmd == 0 || m_timestamp_sent - m_last_data_cmd > tps * 30))
+    {
+      m_link_established = false;
+    }
+
     // Silence the GBA until its link is actually established: the boot jingle
     // otherwise replays on every auto-reset while XD probes. Under netplay,
     // remote players' GBAs additionally stay muted for the whole session so
@@ -113,22 +151,18 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
       m_netplay_pad_is_local = NetPlay::GetPadDetails(m_device_number).is_local;
       m_netplay_locality_cached = true;
     }
-    m_core->SetLinkAudioMuted(!m_link_established ||
+    m_core->SetLinkAudioMuted((!m_link_established && !m_battle_locked) ||
                               (m_netplay_locality_cached && !m_netplay_pad_is_local));
 
-    const bool probing = m_last_cmd == EBufferCommands::CMD_RESET ||
-                         m_last_cmd == EBufferCommands::CMD_STATUS;
-    const bool handshake_active =
-        m_last_data_cmd != 0 && (m_timestamp_sent - m_last_data_cmd) < tps * 8;
-    if (probing && !link_now && !handshake_active && !m_link_established)
+    if (probing && !link_now && !handshake_active && !m_link_established && !m_battle_locked)
     {
-      // Must exceed the slowest reset->link-window-open time or the cooldown
-      // resets the core before Emerald's window ever opens (livelock).
-      // Measured: bundled open-source BIOS 2.35 s, official BIOS 4.78 s --
-      // 6 s clears the worst case with margin. Steady-state reset cadence is
-      // driven by the window_just_closed edge, so this only affects the
-      // bootstrap/missed-edge recovery path.
-      const u64 min_interval = tps * 6;
+      // The floor has to exceed reset->link-window-open time, or the cooldown
+      // resets the core before Emerald's window ever opens (livelock). Measured:
+      // bundled open-source BIOS 2.35 s, official BIOS 4.78 s. But once a window
+      // has actually been seen since the last reset, the core is known to have
+      // booted, so waiting out the worst case again just wastes retries -- the
+      // port can be re-armed as soon as the window is gone.
+      const u64 min_interval = m_window_seen_since_reset ? tps / 2 : tps * 6;
       const bool window_just_closed = m_link_was_enabled;
       const bool cooldown_elapsed =
           m_last_auto_reset == 0 || m_timestamp_sent - m_last_auto_reset > min_interval;
@@ -154,6 +188,7 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
           Pad::SetGBAReset(details.local_pad, true);
         }
         m_last_auto_reset = m_timestamp_sent;
+        m_window_seen_since_reset = false;
       }
     }
     m_link_was_enabled = link_now;
diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
index 3dbb4fd..aff2220 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
@@ -47,6 +47,11 @@ private:
   u64 m_last_data_cmd = 0;
   bool m_link_was_enabled = false;
   bool m_link_established = false;
+  bool m_window_seen_since_reset = false;
+  // Sustained joybus traffic means a real party exchange, not a stray probe.
+  static constexpr u32 DATA_CMDS_FOR_BATTLE = 64;
+  u32 m_data_cmd_count = 0;
+  bool m_battle_locked = false;
   bool m_netplay_pad_is_local = true;
   bool m_netplay_locality_cached = false;
   u16 m_keys = 0;
-- 
2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)

